    {
      "name": "Day 1: Palaces, hanok lanes and the stream",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "Day one stays in central Seoul, moving from the palace to traditional lanes, small shops and an evening stream walk.",
          "show": [
            {
              "card": {
                "big": "DAY 1",
                "title": "Palaces, lanes and the stream",
                "sub": "A full day in central Seoul"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Start early at Gyeongbokgung, then walk through Bukchon and Anguk, browse Insadong, and finish beside Cheonggyecheon.",
          "show": [
            {
              "map": "day-1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Begin at Gyeongbokgung Palace. Arrive early for the grand gates and the changing of the guard at Gwanghwamun Gate.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-seoul-3-day-itinerary.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 1 · MORNING",
            "title": "Gyeongbokgung Palace"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Hanbok wearers get free palace entry, and rental shops are near the station. The palace is closed on Tuesdays, so swap days if needed.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-hanbok-rental-guide.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 1 · MORNING",
            "title": "Hanbok and palace entry"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Walk north into Bukchon’s traditional lanes, then toward Anguk for a café break. Keep your visit unhurried and remember people live here.",
          "show": [
            {
              "photo_query": "Bukchon Hanok Village",
              "require": [
                "bukchon"
              ]
            },
            {
              "photo_query": "Anguk Seoul cafe",
              "require": [
                "anguk"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 1 · MIDDAY",
            "title": "Bukchon and Anguk"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Continue to Insadong for craft shops and tea houses. It is an easy place to browse without planning a long list of individual stops.",
          "show": [
            {
              "photo_query": "Insadong tea houses",
              "require": [
                "insadong"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 1 · AFTERNOON",
            "title": "Insadong"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "End with a walk along Cheonggyecheon. This streamside path gives you a calmer change of pace after a day among busy streets.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "regional-seoul-travel-cheonggyecheon.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 1 · EVENING",
            "title": "Cheonggyecheon Stream"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Day 2: Markets, Myeongdong and Namsan",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "Day two runs from a market breakfast to shopping and street food, then finishes with a sunset view from Namsan.",
          "show": [
            {
              "card": {
                "big": "DAY 2",
                "title": "Markets and a sunset view",
                "sub": "Gwangjang, Myeongdong and Namsan"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Start at Gwangjang Market, head to Myeongdong for the afternoon, and go up to N Seoul Tower for sunset.",
          "show": [
            {
              "map": "day-2"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Have breakfast at Gwangjang Market and try bindaetteok, a mung bean pancake. Browse the stalls, then leave room for more snacks later.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-korea-trip-cost-calculator.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 2 · MORNING",
            "title": "Gwangjang Market"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Spend the afternoon among Myeongdong’s shops and street-food stalls. It is a good place to pause, snack and take the day at your own pace.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-myeongdong-night-market.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 2 · AFTERNOON",
            "title": "Myeongdong"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Head to N Seoul Tower for sunset and the city lights. If you want to visit an observatory, book ahead and check the current details.",
          "show": [
            {
              "card": {
                "big": "DAY 2 · EVENING",
                "title": "N Seoul Tower",
                "sub": "Korea Plainly"
              }
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 2 · EVENING",
            "title": "N Seoul Tower"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Day 3: Hongdae, Yeonnam-dong and the Han River",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "Day three explores west Seoul: relaxed cafés and a railway park first, lively Hongdae next, then an evening by the Han River.",
          "show": [
            {
              "card": {
                "big": "DAY 3",
                "title": "West Seoul and the river",
                "sub": "Cafés, performers and a riverside evening"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Start in Yeonnam-dong, walk through Hongdae, then choose Mangwon or Yeouido Hangang Park for your river stop.",
          "show": [
            {
              "map": "day-3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Yeonnam-dong is known for relaxed cafés and a long park along an old railway line. Take time here before heading next door.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-korea-travel-apps.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 3 · AFTERNOON",
            "title": "Yeonnam-dong"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Hongdae is Seoul’s university area, with street performers, shops and nightlife. Wander the streets, and stay for dinner if the energy suits you.",
          "show": [
            {
              "photo_query": "Hongdae street performers",
              "require": [
                "hongdae"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 3 · LATE AFTERNOON",
            "title": "Hongdae"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Before dinner, go to Mangwon or Yeouido Hangang Park. Yeouido has river cruises after dark, and locals often order fried chicken to the riverbank.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-seoul-5-day-itinerary.jpg"
            },
            {
              "image": "photo-own-fried-chicken-box.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 3 · EVENING",
            "title": "The Han River"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Day 4: Seongsu, Gangnam and Jamsil",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "Day four is your modern Seoul day: converted factories, a giant library, and a high city view before a lakeside walk.",
          "show": [
            {
              "card": {
                "big": "DAY 4",
                "title": "Modern Seoul",
                "sub": "Seongsu, Gangnam and Jamsil"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Begin in Seongsu, cross the river to COEX in Gangnam, then end in Jamsil at Lotte World Tower and Seokchon Lake.",
          "show": [
            {
              "map": "day-4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Seongsu-dong is an old factory district turned into cafés, concept stores and pop-ups. Nearby Seoul Forest makes this a good place to slow down.",
          "show": [
            {
              "photo_query": "Seongsu Seoul cafes",
              "require": [
                "seongsu"
              ]
            },
            {
              "photo_query": "Seoul Forest park",
              "require": [
                "seoul"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 4 · MORNING",
            "title": "Seongsu and Seoul Forest"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Cross the river to COEX mall in Gangnam and see its giant library. Keep this stop simple: browse the space, take a break, and move on.",
          "show": [
            {
              "photo_query": "COEX Starfield Library",
              "require": [
                "coex"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 4 · AFTERNOON",
            "title": "COEX and its library"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Finish at Lotte World Tower in Jamsil. Seoul Sky has one of the city’s best night views; Seokchon Lake is lovely for a walk nearby.",
          "show": [
            {
              "photo_query": "Lotte World Tower Seoul",
              "require": [
                "lotte"
              ]
            },
            {
              "photo_query": "Seokchon Lake Seoul",
              "require": [
                "seokchon"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 4 · EVENING",
            "title": "Jamsil and Seoul Sky"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Want a calmer day? Swap Gangnam for Changdeokgung and its Secret Garden, which is visited by guided tour. Book ahead, then finish at a Korean bathhouse.",
          "show": [
            {
              "photo_query": "Changdeokgung Secret Garden",
              "require": [
                "changdeokgung"
              ]
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 4 · ALTERNATIVE",
            "title": "A quieter palace day"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Day 5: A day trip",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "For the last day, choose one trip beyond Seoul. The best fit depends on whether you want history, island walks, a guided visit or an easy city outing.",
          "show": [
            {
              "card": {
                "big": "DAY 5",
                "title": "Choose a day trip",
                "sub": "One day beyond Seoul"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Here are four options, not four stops to squeeze into one day. Pick one, then check transport and any booking requirements before you go.",
          "show": [
            {
              "card": {
                "big": "DAY 5: A DAY TRIP",
                "title": "Day 5: A day trip",
                "sub": "Korea Plainly"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "The DMZ is the most unusual choice, but visits are by organised tour only. Bring your passport and book ahead.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-dmz-tour-guide.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 5 · OPTION 1",
            "title": "The DMZ"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Suwon is the easiest option to do on your own. Walk along Hwaseong Fortress, about an hour away by subway or train, then find fried chicken near the market.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-day-trips-from-seoul.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 5 · OPTION 2",
            "title": "Suwon"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Choose Nami Island for walks by the river. It is especially appealing in autumn, when the island’s scenery is at its best.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-nami-island-gapyeong.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 5 · OPTION 3",
            "title": "Nami Island"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Incheon is handy if you fly out the next day. Visit Chinatown and Songdo, and make the most of a day that also keeps you near the airport.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "regional-incheon-local-guide-incheon-chinatown.jpg"
            },
            {
              "image": "regional-incheon-travel-songdo-central-park.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "DAY 5 · OPTION 4",
            "title": "Incheon"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Getting around",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "The subway reaches every stop on this plan. Get a transit card when you arrive; transfers between subway and bus are discounted when you use one.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-korea-public-transport-transfers.jpg"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Taxis are good value for late nights or short hops. Use a Korean map app to plan routes and show the driver your destination.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-kakao-t-taxi-korea.jpg"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Good to know",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "For a central base, look at Myeongdong, Jongno or City Hall. Hongdae also suits travelers who want nightlife.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-seoul-neighborhoods-guide.jpg"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Do the busiest sights early, then keep evenings for markets, the river and night views. That rhythm helps the five days feel relaxed.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-first-evening-seoul.jpg"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Book ahead for a DMZ tour, the Secret Garden tour and observatories at sunset. Check current details before you go.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-korea-travel-advisory.jpg"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Mistakes to avoid",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "Three easy mistakes: arriving late at the busiest sights, forgetting palace closing days, and trying to fit every day-trip choice into one day.",
          "show": [
            {
              "list": {
                "heading": "Avoid these",
                "items": [
                  "Start busy sights early",
                  "Check palace closing days",
                  "Choose one day trip"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "image": "photo-korea-travel-mistakes.jpg"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "voice": "Gyeongbokgung closes Tuesdays, and Changdeokgung closes Mondays. Swap your days if needed, and leave a little free time for cafés and wandering.",
          "show": [
            {
              "photo_query": "Gyeongbokgung Palace gates",
              "require": [
                "gyeongbokgung"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Quick questions",
      "segments": [
        {
          "voice": "Is five days enough for Seoul? Yes. You can cover the main sights, several neighborhoods and a day trip without rushing.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "photo-seoul-first-time.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "Q&A",
            "title": "Is five days enough?"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "Where should you stay? Choose somewhere central, such as Myeongdong, Jongno or City Hall, so most days begin with a short ride.",
          "show": [
            {
              "image": "regional-seoul-shopping-myeongdong-shopping-street.jpg"
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "Q&A",
            "title": "Where should you stay?"
          }
        },
        {
          "voice": "What is the best day trip? The DMZ is the most unusual, Suwon is easiest on your own, and Nami Island is best in autumn.",
          "show": [
            {
              "card": {
                "big": "Q&A",
                "title": "Which day trip is best?",
                "sub": "Korea Plainly"
              }
            }
          ],
          "label": {
            "kicker": "Q&A",
            "title": "Which day trip is best?"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
